  "decision_rule": "Fixed before the run (design: Danyil). The answer swap's positive control works if it flips at least 30% of the questions at the last token in at least one band; otherwise a low answer-swap rate at the cue phrase says nothing. If it works, at the cue phrase (24-40), per lens: \"two steps\" if the bridge swap flips more than the answer swap (paired bootstrap 95% CI of bridge - answer above 0) and the answer swap stays near its null; \"shortcut\" if the answer swap flips about as often as the bridge swap (that CI includes 0); \"both\" if both are well above their nulls, in which case the leakage (cosine of the two difference vectors, each edit's share in the other pair's span) decides whether the two swaps are different edits at all."
